1
00:00:04,706 --> 00:00:07,126
(Penny:)Kim, the night manager,
went on maternity leave...

2
00:00:07,292 --> 00:00:09,042
(Penny:)...and her husband's name is Sandy.

3
00:00:09,211 --> 00:00:12,631
(Penny:)So get this, her replacement
is a woman named Sandy...

4
00:00:12,797 --> 00:00:14,927
(Penny:)...whose husband's name is Kim.

5
00:00:17,093 --> 00:00:18,473
[CHORTLING]

6
00:00:18,637 --> 00:00:22,137
(Leonard:)-Wow.
-I know. What are the odds? Oh.

7
00:00:22,307 --> 00:00:26,607
(Sheldon:)Easily calculable. We begin by identifying
the set of couples with unisex names.

8
00:00:26,770 --> 00:00:29,100
We eliminate those unqualified
for restaurant work:

9
00:00:29,272 --> 00:00:31,812
(Sheldon:)the aged, the imprisoned
and the limbless, for example.

10
00:00:31,983 --> 00:00:33,813
-Next, we look at the--
LEONARD: Sheldon.

11
00:00:34,152 --> 00:00:36,992
(Leonard:)It's an amazing coincidence.
Can we leave it at that?

12
00:00:38,657 --> 00:00:40,077
(Sheldon:)I'm sorry.

13
00:00:40,242 --> 00:00:45,742
(Sheldon:)Oh, Penny, it's as if the Cheesecake
Factory is run by witches.

14
00:00:47,832 --> 00:00:51,632
(Penny:)Oh, Sheldon, it's as if you don't think
I'll punch you.

15
00:00:53,213 --> 00:00:55,133
(Leonard:)Come on, you guys. Let it go.

16
00:00:55,298 --> 00:00:57,008
(Penny:)Fine, whatever.

17
00:00:57,175 --> 00:00:58,965
(Penny:)Are you finished?

18
00:00:59,135 --> 00:01:02,095
(Sheldon:)Well, thank you. How thoughtful.

